      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T14:11:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The normal accessor seems to copy the value into a std::string which then doesn\u0027t have any clean up once we\u0027re finished with it so we don\u0027t know where that piece of memory would end up, that was the bit I was trying to avoid.\n\nI\u0027m not sure what it means for properties to have the same context. Will all the processes have the secret mapped into their memory that they could access even if the SELinux rules say they can\u0027t? I assume that\u0027s not the case.",
      "parentUuid": "62a4a2f4_3a83b6af",
      "range": {
